WEBVTT

1
00:00:14.099 --> 00:00:15.780
was a canal near the children's house.

2
00:00:17.581 --> 00:00:20.363
Small boats called barges went up and down the canal.

3
00:00:21.664 --> 00:00:23.285
The boats often carried coal.

4
00:00:24.786 --> 00:00:28.268
Some boats had motors and some were pulled by horses or mules.

5
00:00:31.328 --> 00:00:33.989
The children loved the canal almost as much as the railway.

6
00:00:35.309 --> 00:00:37.410
They loved the railway best for two reasons.

7
00:00:38.470 --> 00:00:43.471
They had found the railway first, and the people who worked on the canal barges were unfriendly.

8
00:00:44.892 --> 00:00:46.772
Once the children had gone fishing in the canal.

9
00:00:47.873 --> 00:00:50.753
But a boy on a barge had thrown a piece of coal at Phyllis.

10
00:00:51.914 --> 00:00:53.114
He'd done it just for fun.

11
00:00:54.394 --> 00:00:55.495
What a nasty boy!

12
00:00:56.355 --> 00:00:59.456
Phyllis said it didn't hurt, but they stopped fishing and went home.

13
00:01:02.052 --> 00:01:05.554
One fine day the three children were walking along the road near the canal.

14
00:01:07.035 --> 00:01:09.336
Peter said, "Let's go fishing again!"

15
00:01:10.737 --> 00:01:12.318
Phyllis remembered the mean boy.

16
00:01:13.098 --> 00:01:17.360
But Peter said, "I'll fight any boys who throw coal at your head, Phyllis!"

17
00:01:19.682 --> 00:01:22.663
So they went down to the path next to the canal and started fishing.

18
00:01:24.364 --> 00:01:26.005
The children fished for half an hour.

19
00:01:26.025 --> 00:01:29.247
"Hey!" said a loud voice.

20
00:01:29.267 --> 00:01:34.593
"Move!" An old white horse walked slowly toward them.

21
00:01:35.714 --> 00:01:36.875
It was pulling a barge.

22
00:01:38.916 --> 00:01:42.158
Bobbie, Peter, and Phyllis jumped off the path and climbed up the hill.

23
00:01:43.258 --> 00:01:46.300
They waited for the barge and the horse to pass so they could keep fishing.

24
00:01:46.320 --> 00:01:49.321
"The barge is staying here!

25
00:01:50.562 --> 00:01:51.643
What rotten luck!"

26
00:01:52.123 --> 00:01:52.683
said Peter.

27
00:01:54.184 --> 00:01:58.066
The man on the barge looked at them and said angrily, "What are you staring at?"

28
00:01:58.086 --> 00:02:02.416
"We weren't staring," said Bobbie.

29
00:02:02.436 --> 00:02:03.277
"Well, go away!"

30
00:02:03.757 --> 00:02:04.338
said the man.

31
00:02:04.358 --> 00:02:06.920
"We can stay here.

32
00:02:08.001 --> 00:02:09.802
We're not bothering anyone!"

33
00:02:10.202 --> 00:02:10.823
said Phyllis.

34
00:02:12.224 --> 00:02:13.285
"You're bothering me!"

35
00:02:13.705 --> 00:02:14.265
said the man.

36
00:02:15.426 --> 00:02:17.768
He got off his barge and started to climb the hill.

37
00:02:19.329 --> 00:02:20.710
The children were a little scared.

38
00:02:21.831 --> 00:02:25.434
The bargeman grabbed Peter's leg and said, "You can't fish in the canal.

39
00:02:26.435 --> 00:02:27.716
And don't be so cheeky!"

40
00:02:31.136 --> 00:02:33.697
Bobbie came down the hill a little and talked to the bargeman.

41
00:02:33.717 --> 00:02:36.358
"Please don't be angry with Peter.

42
00:02:37.299 --> 00:02:38.339
We won't fish anymore."

43
00:02:38.359 --> 00:02:40.120
"All right then.

44
00:02:40.820 --> 00:02:42.521
Now go home," he replied.

45
00:02:44.041 --> 00:02:45.562
The man went down to his barge.

46
00:02:45.582 --> 00:02:47.943
"Give me a coat, Maria!"

47
00:02:48.323 --> 00:02:48.883
he shouted.

48
00:02:50.244 --> 00:02:52.585
A red-haired woman with a baby threw a coat at him.

49
00:02:53.745 --> 00:02:56.086
"I'll be at the pub, the Rose and Crown.

50
00:02:57.247 --> 00:02:59.708
Meet me there when the baby's asleep," he said.

51
00:03:00.948 --> 00:03:03.831
When the bargeman had gone, the children climbed down the hill.

52
00:03:03.851 --> 00:03:08.094
"I think the canal belongs to everyone," Peter said.

53
00:03:09.615 --> 00:03:11.297
The woman got off the boat and saw them.

54
00:03:11.317 --> 00:03:14.659
"Don't worry about Bill," she said.

55
00:03:14.679 --> 00:03:17.342
"He gets angry quickly.

56
00:03:19.043 --> 00:03:20.504
He'll be back in two hours.

57
00:03:21.605 --> 00:03:23.707
You can catch fish now," she said.

58
00:03:23.727 --> 00:03:26.329
"Thank you," said Bobbie.

59
00:03:26.349 --> 00:03:28.130
"You're kind.

60
00:03:28.851 --> 00:03:29.692
Where's your baby?"

61
00:03:30.988 --> 00:03:33.249
"Asleep in the cabin," she replied.

62
00:03:33.269 --> 00:03:35.110
"He'll be fine.

63
00:03:35.930 --> 00:03:38.051
He's safe in there, and the dog's with him."

64
00:03:39.431 --> 00:03:43.373
The woman left, and Peter fished for a while, but he didn't catch anything.

65
00:03:44.734 --> 00:03:46.774
It was nearly dark, and the girls were tired.

66
00:03:47.555 --> 00:03:49.856
Suddenly Phyllis cried, "What's that?"

67
00:03:50.176 --> 00:03:51.336
She pointed to the barge.

68
00:03:52.457 --> 00:03:53.697
Smoke poured from the doors.

69
00:03:58.319 --> 00:04:00.700
"The bargeman's boat is on fire, that's all.

70
00:04:01.668 --> 00:04:02.408
I'm glad!"

71
00:04:02.829 --> 00:04:03.369
said Peter.

72
00:04:03.389 --> 00:04:06.570
"Peter, how can you say that?"

73
00:04:06.871 --> 00:04:07.511
cried Phyllis.

74
00:04:07.531 --> 00:04:10.092
"Think of the poor dog!"

75
00:04:10.112 --> 00:04:12.073
"And the baby!"

76
00:04:12.413 --> 00:04:13.534
Bobbie suddenly screamed.

77
00:04:14.654 --> 00:04:17.115
All three children ran to the barge as fast as they could.
